; DECIMAL RENDERING OF AN ARBITRARY-PRECISION VALUE, written in Oroboros.
;
; The first real text program in this language, and it exists to answer a
; question string-operations.md could not: does a text program INDEX a string,
; or only fold it? That decides whether a string has to become an indexable
; table (and pay UTF-32) or can stay the free monoid it is.
;
; THE ANSWER IS THAT IT FOLDS. Every string here is built by `concat` out of
; one-scalar strings; nothing is indexed, nothing needs a length, and nothing
; compares two strings. Three operations — `concat`, `""` and η — and every one
; of them is derived from the free monoid rather than chosen.
;
; It is also the arithmetic half of what windows has been missing: that host can
; compute an arbitrary-precision value and cannot print one, and printing is
; repeated division by a power of ten, which `div-small` and `rem-small` are.
;
;   x % 10^8   is `big%-small`, whose result is a machine WORD
;   x / 10^8   is `big/` by a widened word, one pass
;
; The group size is 10^8 rather than 10^9 because `div-small`'s column is
; `r * 2^24 + limb`, which stays inside ADR 0012's window only for a divisor
; under about 2^28 — and nothing here states that, because bounded-by-default
; asks at the call site with the caller's own range in hand.

(export render)

; ---------------------------------------------------------------- one group
;
; Eight decimal digits of a machine word, most significant first, built by
; PREPENDING each digit to what is already there — which is the monoid operation
; and the reason no index is ever needed.
;
; `pad` says whether this is an interior group, which keeps its leading zeros,
; or the most significant one, which does not. The two cases differ only in a
; guard, so there is one `again` (ADR 0015).
(def group (fn (d pad)
  (loop ((s "") (k 0) (r d))
    (>= k 8)                              s
    (and (not pad) (and (= r 0) (> k 0))) s
    else (again (concat (string-of (+ 48 (% r 10))) s) (+ k 1) (/ r 10)))))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------- the value
;
; Least significant group first, each PREPENDED, so the result comes out in
; order without anything ever being indexed or reversed.
;
; The trip bound is what makes this terminate provably: `v` shrinks by a factor
; of 10^8 each time, and nothing can bound a big value's magnitude from its
; structure, so the program says how many groups there can be. That is
; `tree.oro`'s node cap again — a capacity does not create the limit, it makes
; it visible.
(def digits (fn (x)
  (loop ((s "") (v x) (i 0))
    (= v 0)   s
    (>= i 32) s
    else (let (/ v 100000000) (fn (nv)
           (again (concat (group (% v 100000000) (> nv 0)) s) nv (+ i 1)))))))

(sig render ((x (int 0 (pow 2 200)))) string)
(def render (fn (x) (if (= x 0) "0" (digits x))))
